{title: Cornerstone}
{subtitle: Eckstein}
{song_number: 142}
{language: en}
{tempo: 72}
{key: E}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[E]My hope is built on nothing less [A]than Jesus' blood and [B]righteousness.
[C#m7]I dare not trust the sweetest [E]frame, [A]but wholly [B]trust in [E]Jesus' Name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[E]When darkness seems to hide His face, [A]I rest on His unchanging [B]grace.
[C#m7]In every high and stormy [E]gale, [A]my anchor [B]holds with[E]in the veil.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Christ alone, [C#m]Corner[B]stone. [E/G#]Weak made
[A]strong in the [C#m]Saviour's [B]love. [E]Through the [A]storm, He [C#m]is [B]Lord,
[B]Lord of [E]all.
[C#m]He is Lord, [B]Lord of [A]all.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[E]When He shall come with trumpet sound, oh may I then in Him be found.
Dressed in His righteousness alone. Faultless stand before the throne.
{end_of_verse}
